<title>USA: TABLE-Columbus McKinnon Q1 pro forma net up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Columbus McKinnon Q1 pro forma net up.</headline>
<text>
<p>BUFFALO, N.Y., July 22 /PRNewswire/ -- Columbus McKinnon</p>
<p>						    Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					6/29/97</p>
<p>					Actual and	   6/30/96</p>
<p>					Pro Forma	Actual  Pro Forma</p>
<p>Net sales			 $124,442	$65,735     $116,711</p>
<p>Cost of products sold	   89,239*	45,718	 81,829</p>
<p>Gross Profit			35,203	 20,017	 34,882</p>
<p>Gross profit margin		28.3%	  30.5%	  29.9%</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p> administrative expense	 17,508*	10,894	 17,857</p>
<p>Income from operations before</p>
<p> amortization		     17,695	  9,123	 17,025</p>
<p>Amortization			 2,549	    442	  2,578</p>
<p>Income from operations	  15,146	  8,681	 14,447</p>
<p>Interest and other</p>
<p> expense, net			6,209	     73	  6,262</p>
<p>Income before income taxes     8,937	  8,608	  8,185</p>
<p>Income tax expense		 4,506	  3,576	  3,898</p>
<p>Net income			   4,431	  5,032	  4,287</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding    13,360	 13,200	 13,200</p>
<p>Primary and fully diluted</p>
<p> income per share		  $0.33	  $0.38	  $0.32</p>
<p>(In thousands, except per share and percentage data)</p>
<p>NOTES: Full name is Columbus McKinnon Corp.</p>
<p>* Includes reclassification $1.9 million to cost of products sold from administrative expense to put division account classifications on internally consistent basis.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
